## Concept
- Product: Drishti, the pose distribution platform. You buy asanas during seasonal
  sales, they sit uninstalled in your backlog, and Chair Pose has been Mostly Negative
  since 2019.
- Demo: Steam-style library client. Searchable/sortable sidebar of owned poses with
  hours practiced (mostly near zero), detail pane with review histogram, achievements,
  patch notes, and a Practice Now install bar that stalls at 91% on
  "Verifying integrity of hips..." before completing.

## Design direction
- Style: game-storefront library console, incense-dark slate mode. Capsule cards,
  matcha discount corner tags, review histogram bars, tag chips, hours-played
  counters, build numbers.
- Palette: Incense Slate / Sale Matcha. primary #5FA8D3 (tranquil steam blue),
  accent #A9BE55 (discount tags + Overwhelmingly Positive only), bg #151C26,
  fg #E8EDF2, muted #77879B, ink #EAF0F6.
- Fonts: Marcellus (display, Roman inscriptional serif) / Inter (body) /
  Space Mono (telemetry).
- Anti-sameness: checked against the last 7 entries (neuralink-sommeliers,
  anduril-gen-z, doordash-squirrels, neuralink-goats, peloton-koalas,
  tiktok-night-owls, slack-foxes). No collision on style, palette, or font pairing;
  deliberately avoided gold-on-dark (sommeliers), green-on-dark (koalas), and all
  recently used display faces and monos.

## Images
- Rationale: demo is photo-shaped (pose capsule art, i.e. game covers), so the
  4-image budget went to capsules: 1 hero Featured & Recommended capsule (crow,
  1600x900) + 3 library capsules (savasana, headstand, chair, 800x450). Testimonial
  headshots skipped so all three review cards keep consistent initials badges.
- crow.webp: attempt 1, judge PASS (correct bakasana, palette match, no text).
- savasana.webp: attempt 1, judge PASS (correct corpse pose, incense haze on brand).
- headstand.webp: attempt 1, judge PASS; slight motion blur at the feet reads as
  intended Early Access wobble. Needed one extra script invocation after a
  transient API 503 (the failed call produced no image).
- chair.webp: attempt 1, judge PASS (correct utkatasana; the script's internal
  retry absorbed another 503).
- API calls used: 5 of 10 daily cap (4 successful generations + 1 failed 503 call).

